  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting India&#x2019;s Progress Towards 95-95-95 through EMTCT, Interventions among Incarcerated Populations, Integrated Service Delivery for High Risk and Bridge populations and systems strengthening - India (01-Apr-2021-31-Mar-2024)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">India, HIV, Solidarity and Action Against The HIV Infection in India (SAATHII)This program has the following goals: Achieving zero new infections, zero AIDS-related deaths and zero AIDS related stigma &amp; discrimination. The objectives of this program are: Reduce new infections by 80% by 2024.  Link 95% of estimated PLHIV to services by 2024.  Ensure ART initiation and retention of 95% PLHIV for sustained viral suppression by 2024.  Eliminate mother-to-child transmission of HIV and syphilis by 2020.  Eliminate HIV/AIDS related stigma and discrimination by 2020.  Facilitate sustainable NACP service delivery by 2024</narrative>
  </description>
